---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { HEATS } from '../data/taxonomy';
---
<Base title="About" description="What Qualified Ledes is, who it is for, and how stories are picked and written.">
  <main id="content" class="prose">
    <h1 class="display">About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p>{SITE.name} is a daily marketing news page for small businesses, nonprofits and the marketers who serve them. Every story answers three questions: what changed, why it matters, and what to do about it.</p>
    <h2 class="display">Two kinds of readers</h2>
    <p><strong>Main Street</strong> stories are for business owners and nonprofit teams who do their own marketing. <strong>Trade Desk</strong> stories are for marketers, freelancers and agencies who do it for others. Some stories are for both. Use the Reader filter to see only yours, or go straight to the page <a href="/for/small-business/">for small businesses and nonprofits</a> or the page <a href="/for/marketers/">for marketers and agencies</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="display">How hot is it?</h2>
    <ul>
      {HEATS.map((h) => <li><strong>{h.label}:</strong> {h.meaning}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <h2 class="display">How stories are picked</h2>
    <p>New stories are added every day, once or twice a day, from trade press, platform announcements, research and local business news. Summaries are written in our own words, and every story links to its original source so you can read the full piece.</p>
    <p>Each week we publish a roundup of the best stories, and an email version is coming soon. <a href="/subscribe/">Join the early list</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="display" id="angie">Who is behind it</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is curated by {SITE.author}. {SITE.authorBio}</p>
    <p>Find Angie on <a href={SITE.authorLinkedIn} rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a> or at <a href={SITE.authorUrl} rel="me noopener">angieconnelly.com</a>.</p>
    <p>Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>, or <a href="/contact/">send a tip or correction</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
